  "boardChanges": [
    {
      "line": 228,
      "before": "| 4 | `B51` | Shared contract drafted; Zorg resolved mode and namespace intent, while instance-binding lifetime remains open | [Draft](design/direct-peer-send.md) proposes explicit restricted sending, immutable association and one-hop enforcement; [response](reviews/direct-peer-send-draft-response.md) asks Zorg to agree a distinct instance binding or complete retirement rule before final types and design approval |",
      "after": "| 4 | `B51` | Zorg accepts the instance binding and public shape; AGP design review and lease-lifecycle integration remain | [Reconciled draft](design/direct-peer-send.md) carries D61's agreement; [lifecycle response](reviews/direct-peer-send-lifecycle-response.md) identifies the missing pending-use/session observation contract, to resolve with B6 owners before production lease integration |"
    },
    {
      "line": 294,
      "before": "Status: the scale amendment is drafted, not ratified; the direct-peer send contract is drafted with Zorg's explicit mode and namespace choices, while instance-binding lifetime, API review and the joint credential lifecycle remain open.\\",
      "after": "Status: the scale amendment is drafted, not ratified; Zorg has accepted the direct-peer instance binding and public shape, while AGP design review, declared lease-lifecycle integration and the joint credential lifecycle remain open.\\"
    },
    {
      "line": 302,
      "before": "| `B51` | Review the direct-peer send draft and agree instance-binding lifetime with Zorg | [Draft and new reply](VERIFICATION.md#450-direct-peer-send-draft-and-zorg-lifetime-review) separate caller timeout from late host replies; a non-secret instance-binding identifier is proposed, not agreed; public types, shared enforcement and consumer acceptance remain unbuilt, and server push is deferred |",
      "after": "| `B51` | Review the reconciled direct-peer design and resolve the declared lease-lifecycle boundary with B6 owners | [D61 reconciliation](VERIFICATION.md#451-direct-peer-agreement-and-lease-lifecycle-boundary) records consumer agreement and the current snapshot mismatch; public types, shared enforcement and consumer acceptance remain unbuilt, and server push is deferred |"
    },
    {
      "line": 344,
      "before": "| Will admission supply a distinct instance-binding identifier, or establish retirement of every old reply authority before node identity reuse? | `B51` final association and implementation; the [draft](design/direct-peer-send.md) incorporates Zorg's mode and namespace decisions, but its caller-bound retention rule does not establish host reply retirement; public API and design review remain, and ordinary D26 behavior is unchanged |",
      "after": "| What declared lifecycle contract proves a binding has no outstanding credential, pending admission or live session before issuer reclamation? | `B51`/`B6` production lease integration and final design approval; [D61 reconciliation](VERIFICATION.md#451-direct-peer-agreement-and-lease-lifecycle-boundary) records the selected instance binding and public shape, but current connection snapshots do not supply the assumed association; ordinary D26 behavior is unchanged |"
    }
  ],
